From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Leung <lrd.airoha@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 22 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: fix wcid teardown ordering in mt76_reset_device

mt76_reset_device() ran mt76_wcid_cleanup() while the wcid was still
published in dev->wcid[i], only clearing the pointer afterwards.  During
cleanup the wcid is therefore still reachable by concurrent lookups (TX
status, RX), which can grab and use a wcid that is being torn down.

Unpublish first: NULL dev->wcid[i], then run mt76_wcid_cleanup().  This
mirrors the correct add ordering (publish last) so no new lookup can find
the wcid once teardown has begun.

Signed-off-by: Ryan Leung <lrd.airoha@gmail.com>
---
--- a/mac80211.c
+++ b/mac80211.c
@@ -856,8 +856,8 @@ void mt76_reset_device(struct mt76_dev *dev)
 			continue;

 		wcid->sta = 0;
-		mt76_wcid_cleanup(dev, wcid);
 		rcu_assign_pointer(dev->wcid[i], NULL);
+		mt76_wcid_cleanup(dev, wcid);
 	}
 	rcu_read_unlock();
